From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:11:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple: power the J604's empty SD reader port
 down by default

Turn pcie_apple.t8132_sd_port_off on by default, so the J604 keeps its
SD reader off with no card in, as macOS does: macOS reads the reader's
root port and endpoint as all ones with the slot empty, and sees a card
through the SMC's card detect while the reader has no power.

Only a port whose node has card-detect-gpios is affected (the J604's
port02). Writing 0 to the parameter brings the reader back up at once,
and a card still powers it up, trains the link and rescans.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index a77e68a451..5998fc7ad3 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(radio_l1ss,
 /* The card reader ports whose slot can power them down (apple_pcie_sd_init()). */
 static LIST_HEAD(apple_pcie_sd_ports);
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(apple_pcie_sd_lock);
-static bool t8132_sd_port_off;
+static bool t8132_sd_port_off = true;
 static int apple_pcie_sd_param_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp);
 static const struct kernel_param_ops apple_pcie_sd_param_ops = {
 	.set = apple_pcie_sd_param_set,
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@ static const struct kernel_param_ops apple_pcie_sd_param_ops = {
 };
 module_param_cb(t8132_sd_port_off, &apple_pcie_sd_param_ops, &t8132_sd_port_off, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132_sd_port_off,
-		 "J604: power the SD card reader's port down while the slot is empty and up again when a card is inserted, as macOS does (default off)");
+		 "J604: power the SD card reader's port down while the slot is empty and up again when a card is inserted, as macOS does (default on)");
 
 #define APPLE_PCIE_T8132_EXP		0x70	/* the root port's PCIe capability */
 
@@ -2941,7 +2941,7 @@ static int apple_pcie_port_reset_endpoint(struct apple_pcie *pcie,
 }
 
 /*
- * A card reader port powered down while its slot is empty (pcie_apple.t8132_sd_port_off, off by
+ * A card reader port powered down while its slot is empty (pcie_apple.t8132_sd_port_off, on by
  * default). On the J604 macOS keeps the SD reader's link off with no card in: its root port and
  * endpoint read all ones, and the Apple device tree routes the slot's card detect to an SMC
  * input, so the card is seen while the reader itself has no power. With the parameter on, an
